# Intake disposition word-boundary fix — apply ladder

The acceptance-smoke RE-RUN after the #172 LLM intent-extraction seal
(`docs/experiments/loam-1.0-acceptance-smoke-rerun8.md`) surfaced a residual
gap on variant A: the role-play opener "I spend two hours every night writing
up the listing descriptions … I'd love to just… not do that anymore" was
classified START — because `_detect_disposition`'s START token "more" matched
the TAIL of "any-more". loam fed back the INVERTED proposal ("help you
reliably GET TO writing …"), the user had to correct it, and seven soft
dimensions FAILed off that single inversion.

A CLEAR-DIRECTION fix, not a design fork — and a PRE-EXISTING latent bug
(verified present on BASELINE b8817c71, NOT a regression from the #172 seam).
`_detect_disposition` now matches stop/start tells on WORD BOUNDARIES so
"more" never matches inside "anymore", and reads cessation phrasings
("not … anymore", "no longer", "off my plate", "sick of", "tired of",
"done with") as STOP; a tie favours STOP (the cessation tell is the stronger
intent). Genuine STARTs ("I want to start journaling", "I should do more
reviews") still read START.

